DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("ln((3*x))");
$fun_1 = Formula("((ln(x)))^(1/2)");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-9, -4, -1, 10} U ({-9, -4, -1, 10} U {-10, -3, -2, 1, 3} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-9, -4, -1, 10}))");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-10, -3, -2, 1, 3} U {-10, -3, -2, 1, 3}");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(7, infinity) U (7, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (7, infinity)) U (({-8, -4, 3, 5, 6, 7}) U (((-infinity, 10] U ((((-infinity, 10]))))) U (({-8, -4, 3, 5, 6, 7} U (-infinity, 10] U (-infinity, 10])) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (7, infinity)))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(({-8, -4, 3, 5, 6, 7})) U (7, infinity)");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("((-infinity, 10] - {-8, -4, 3, 5, 6, 7})");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`8/11+7`] is equal to [_____]{Formula('7.72727272727')}
---

What is the value of [`1+5+0+3/9`]? [_____]{Real(6.33333333333)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \leq 10\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 6\}`]
- [`C = \{-8, -4, 3, 5, 6, 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup B \cap B \cup ((C) \cup ((A \cup (((A))))) \cup ((C \cup A \cup A)) \cap B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`((C)) \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`A - C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-10, -3, -2, 1, 3\}`]
- [`B = \{-9, -4, -1, 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup (B \cup A \cap B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 8, 6, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -4, 0, -1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -6, 10, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, 0, -1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-6, 10, -5>") . Compute("<8, 6, 2>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-4, 0, -1>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-4, 0, -1>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<8, 6, 2>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<8, 6, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -8, 7, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 7, -10, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-8, 7, -5>") x Compute("<7, -10, -5>")}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-8, 7, -5>") . Compute("<7, -10, -5>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-8, 7, -5>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, -10, -5>") . Compute("<-8, 7, -5>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>2)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
